It is important to note that the simplified polar_encode and polar_decode functions used in this simulation do not implement the full complexity of state-of-the-art Polar Code algorithms (e.g., successive cancellation list decoding or optimized construction). Therefore, the presented BER performance serves as a conceptual demonstration rather than a benchmark for highly optimized Polar Codes. A more sophisticated implementation would yield significantly better BER performance, closer to theoretical limits.
VI. Conclusion
This paper has explored the feasibility of employing Polar Codes for satellite communication, encompassing theoretical foundations, Python-based implementation, GNU Radio integration, and USRP hardware considerations. We have demonstrated the conceptual framework for simulating Polar Code performance and outlined the necessary steps for deploying such systems in a software-defined radio environment.
The capacity-achieving properties and low complexity of Polar Codes make them a compelling choice for future satellite communication systems, particularly in scenarios demanding high spectral efficiency and robust error correction. While the Python implementation provided herein is simplified, it serves as a valuable starting point for further development and optimization of Polar Code algorithms.
The integration with GNU Radio and USRP hardware provides a powerful and flexible platform for both research and practical deployment. This SDR-centric approach allows for rapid prototyping, testing, and real-time experimentation with advanced coding schemes, accelerating the development cycle for next-generation satellite communication technologies.
Future work will focus on implementing more advanced Polar Code construction and decoding algorithms (e.g., SCL decoding), optimizing the Python code for performance, and conducting extensive real-time over-the-air experiments using USRP hardware to validate the theoretical and simulated performance in diverse satellite channel conditions. Further research will also delve into the latency aspects of Polar Code decoding for real-time SDR-based transmission.
